      "problem": "Expand $(3p - 5)^2.$",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the following formula:\n\n$$\n(a-b)^2 = a^2 - 2ab + b^2\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=3p$ and $b=5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t(3p - 5)^2 &= \\\n\t\t(3p)^2 - 2(3p)(5) + 5^2 &= \\\n\t\t9p^2 - 30p + 25.\n\t}\n$$",
